<title>SINGAPORE: UIC 1996 net profit rises 10 pct.</title>
<headline>UIC 1996 net profit rises 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			68.62  vs    62.16</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)	     1.0   vs     1.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		5.1   vs     4.6</p>
<p>    Turnover			 336.82  vs   326.78</p>
<p>    Investment income		0.60  vs     0.84</p>
<p>    Other income		     5.48  vs     8.65</p>
<p>    Interest expense		17.64  vs    20.56</p>
<p>    Operating pretax	     108.60  vs   102.50</p>
<p>    Associates			22.81  vs    18.83</p>
<p>    Income tax			25.72  vs    23.51</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (37.07) vs   (35.67)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  0.98  vs     1.54</p>
<p>    Dividend pay/register	 July 3 /June 18</p>
<p>Note -- United Industrial Corp Ltd said it made a group extraordinary gain of Singapore S$984,000 on the disposal of factory premises. On the company level, there was a S$56.87 million extraordinary gain from the liquidation and sale of subsidiary companies.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
